        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>A Tale of Two Cultures</title>\n<style>\n    body {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 20px;\n        background-color: #fff;\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: center;\n    }\n    .page-wrapper {\n        width: 950px;\n        position: relative;\n        background-color: #fff;\n        padding: 30px;\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    .top-text {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 10px;\n        left: 45px;\n        font-family: monospace;\n        font-size: 11px;\n        color: #000;\n        letter-spacing: 1px;\n        white-space: pre;\n    }\n    .reg-mark {\n        position: absolute;\n        width: 14px;\n        height: 14px;\n        border: 1px solid #000;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n    }\n    .reg-mark::before {\n        content: '';\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 6px;\n        left: -8px;\n        width: 30px;\n        height: 1px;\n        background: #000;\n    }\n    .reg-mark::after {\n        content: '';\n        position: absolute;\n        left: 6px;\n        top: -8px;\n        width: 1px;\n        height: 30px;\n        background: #000;\n    }\n    .top-center { top: 5px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); }\n    .bottom-center { bottom: 5px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); }\n    .left-center { left: 5px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); }\n    .right-center { right: 5px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); }\n\n    .grey-box {\n        background-color: #a6a6a6;\n        padding: 60px 40px 70px 40px;\n        position: relative;\n        margin-top: 20px;\n    }\n    .parody-container {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 0;\n        right: 120px;\n        width: 250px;\n        height: 45px;\n        overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .parody-text {\n        position: absolute;\n        bottom: -20px;\n        right: 0;\n        font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n        font-size: 90px;\n        font-weight: bold;\n        color: #111;\n    }\n    .main-title {\n        text-align: center;\n        font-family: \"Arial Black\", Impact, sans-serif;\n        font-size: 54px;\n        color: #222;\n        margin: 20px 0 5px 0;\n        letter-spacing: -1.5px;\n    }\n    .sub-title {\n        text-align: center;\n        font-family: \"Arial Black\", Impact, sans-serif;\n        font-size: 28px;\n        color: #222;\n        margin: 0 0 45px 0;\n        letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n    }\n    .articles-container {\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: space-between;\n        gap: 25px;\n    }\n    .article-box {\n        background-color: #fff;\n        border: 1px solid #000;\n        box-shadow: 12px 12px 0px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);\n        width: 48%;\n        padding: 25px 20px;\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n        display: flex;\n        flex-direction: column;\n    }\n    .logo-le-monde {\n        text-align: center;\n        font-family: \"Old English Text MT\", \"Engravers Old English\", \"UnifrakturMaguntia\", serif;\n        font-size: 46px;\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\n        color: #000;\n    }\n    .logo-washington-times {\n        text-align: center;\n        font-family: \"Old English Text MT\", \"Engravers Old English\", \"UnifrakturMaguntia\", serif;\n        font-size: 36px;\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\n        color: #000;\n    }\n    .sep-line {\n        border-top: 3px solid #000;\n        margin: 0 0 20px 0;\n    }\n    .sep-line-thick {\n        border-top: 4px solid #000;\n        margin: 0;\n    }\n    .author-box {\n        text-align: center;\n        font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n        font-weight: bold;\n        font-size: 15px;\n        padding: 6px 0;\n        letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n    }\n    .content-grid {\n        display: flex;\n        gap: 15px;\n        flex-grow: 1;\n    }\n    .col {\n        flex: 1;\n        font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n        font-size: 13px;\n        line-height: 1.3;\n        text-align: justify;\n    }\n    .article-heading {\n        font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n        font-size: 38px;\n        font-weight: bold;\n        line-height: 1;\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\n        letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n    }\n    p {\n        margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n        text-indent: 15px;\n    }\n    p.no-indent {\n        text-indent: 0;\n    }\n    .signature-block {\n        margin-top: 15px;\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n    .sig-name {\n        font-weight: bold;\n        font-style: italic;\n        font-size: 13px;\n    }\n    .sig-date {\n        font-style: italic;\n        font-size: 12px;\n    }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"page-wrapper\">\n        <div class=\"top-text\">Iss. 40/June 22 parody  1/21/02 2:20 PM  Page 1</div>\n        \n        <div class=\"reg-mark top-center\"></div>\n        <div class=\"reg-mark bottom-center\"></div>\n        <div class=\"reg-mark left-center\"></div>\n        <div class=\"reg-mark right-center\"></div>\n        \n        <div class=\"grey-box\">\n            <div class=\"parody-container\">\n                <div class=\"parody-text\">Parody</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"main-title\">A Tale of Two Cultures</div>\n            <div class=\"sub-title\">How Two Newspapers Cover the World Cup</div>\n            \n            <div class=\"articles-container\">\n                <!-- Le Monde Article -->\n                <div class=\"article-box\">\n                    <div class=\"logo-le-monde\">Le Monde</div>\n                    <div class=\"sep-line\"></div>\n                    \n                    <div class=\"content-grid\">\n                        <div class=\"col\">\n                            <div class=\"article-heading\">Allemagne<br>v. Etats-<br>Unis</div>\n                            <p>The green field at Parc des Princes shimmered like the lips of the virgin spring, unmistakably French, innocent yet knowing, a totality bursting upon a completion. Across its surface, 22 men—non-French, non-significant—scampered after a black and white ball, their existence overshadowed by the deep wisdom of the French soil, the chic of the grass. This reporter sat in the press box munching a biscuit, remembering the soft smells of his nursemaid so many years ago in Deauville.</p>\n                            <p>As the game commenced, the score was nothingness to nothingness. The ball was</p>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"col\">\n                            <p class=\"no-indent\">round with that marvelous roundness that round things have when they are in France. The Germans, paradoxes of angst and <i>Anschluss</i>, pushed from East to West (ironic echo of their Austrian cousins at Austerlitz!). Meanwhile, the Americans, vulgar, commercial, yet vital in their childish way, stood hapless before the Hessian onslaught. The score may have changed as the match progressed, but is a goal an addition or a subtraction? Is it not a slavish concession to the bourgeois production ethic? Does it not mar the Hellenic perfection of the spheric zero? Is a ball in the back of the net a mere construct played upon by the ever-shifting fancy of our perceptions? Up in the press box, I sneezed, and the entire Yale English faculty got a cold....</p>\n                            <div class=\"signature-block\">\n                                <div class=\"sig-name\">Pierre Henri-Lévy Derrida</div>\n                                <div class=\"sig-date\">(Mercredi 27 mai.)</div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                \n                <!-- The Washington Times Article -->\n                <div class=\"article-box\">\n                    <div class=\"logo-washington-times\">The Washington Times</div>\n                    <div class=\"sep-line-thick\"></div>\n                    <div class=\"author-box\">BY PATRICK J. BUCHANAN</div>\n                    <div class=\"sep-line-thick\" style=\"margin-bottom: 15px;\"></div>\n                    \n                    <div class=\"content-grid\">\n                        <div class=\"col\">\n                            <div class=\"article-heading\">United<br>States v.<br>Germany</div>\n                            <p>American soldiers with names like O'Brien and O'Malley didn't die at Verdun and Bastogne so a bunch of Huns with names like Klinsmann and Mattheus could shoot soccer balls past American goalies. But, my friends, that's where America's elites have led us—into the clutches of a bunch of thick-thighed Hessians with devious elbows.</p>\n                            <p>It may not occur to the pansy mandarins of the corporate class, but American greatness was built on the premise that God gave us arms, and we should use them. The rest of the world is filled with dim-witted dribblers—half of whom don't even have last names—who no sooner see a ball flying through the air than they want to stick their foreheads in its way. Meanwhile, their hordes of</p>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"col\">\n                            <p class=\"no-indent\">fans—whose lives consist of riots interrupted by welfare checks—jump up and down screeching their idiotic anthems. The full lyrics of one of their soccer songs is this: \"Oh-lay, oh-lay, oh-lay, oh-lay.\" They sound like a bunch of banshees worshiping a potato chip.</p>\n                            <p>So the nation of Mark McGwire and Michael Jordan finds itself sucking up to Yugoslavia and the Netherlands in this quadrennial soccerfest. How did we get into this position? The answer is that the World Cup is the sports equivalent of the GATT: big, multicultural, run by hairless global bureaucrats, and organized to create the greatest possible humiliation for the American working man. And the global elites, who check their loyalties at the airport Gold Club lounges, want to merge our identity into some cosmopolitan cocktail reception. Whenever I see an American calling this game \"football,\" I want to puke.</p>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
